    "label": {
      "en": "Rate for employee old-age insurance contributions (whole income)"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tsceepi_rate2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This is the 0.40% rate applied to employee old-age insurance contributions on the whole (uncapped) income, used as the Band_Rate parameter of the 'Old Age insurance contributions' SchedCalc in policy tscee_fr for the income band above income group A's ceiling, where only this whole-income component continues to be levied (the group-A specific 6.90% component no longer applies). The Contributions theme note lists 'Old age' employee contribution rates of 6.90% on income group A and 0.40% on whole income, and this constant corresponds to the latter."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Parameters for employee social insurance contributions"
    },
